<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal- Spot markets quiet, basis up.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal- Spot markets quiet, basis up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal markets were quiet with some offers edging higher amid a smattering of demand for prompt shipment, dealers said.</p>
<p>Crush levels have stabilized with dealers expecting the weekly National Oilseeds Processors Association crush at about 25 million bushels versus 25.043 million a week ago.</p>
<p>Crushers were offering June and July soymeal at a slight premium to spot values because they are concerned about tight soybean supplies this summer. Tight supply concerns also prevented crushers from offering soymeal for August and September positions.</p>
